extends layout

include partials/footer

block content
  main.legal(data-screen-label="Privacy")
    .wrap.legal__inner
      a.legal__home(href="/") ← Buried Worlds

      .section-head
        .ornament
          span.rule
          span.diamond
          span.rule
        h1.h2 Privacy
        p.serif-italic What we collect, which is very little, and what we do with it.

      .legal__body
        p.legal__meta Last updated 27 August 2026

        p
          | Buried Worlds is published by MELVIA PTY. LTD. (ACN 159 295 824,
          | ABN 41 159 295 824), trading as Bellare Studios, of 372/585 Little
          | Collins Street, Melbourne, Victoria 3000, Australia. This policy
          | covers the game on Meta Quest and, from its release, on Steam for
          | PC VR, and it covers this website. Privacy questions and requests
          | go to #[a(href="mailto:privacy@buriedworlds.com") privacy@buriedworlds.com].

        h2.legal__h The short version
        p.
          The game does not have accounts, does not show ads, and contains no
          analytics or tracking software. It runs fully offline once installed,
          it does not know who you are, and it never asks for your name, email
          address or location. Your progress is a file on your own headset and
          never leaves it. The one thing the game ever sends us is feedback you
          choose to send, from a form you have to go and open yourself.
        p.
          This website is separate: it asks you for nothing — there is no
          sign-up form and no mailing list — but it does use Google Analytics
          to count visits, which sets cookies. That is the only tracking
          anywhere in Buried Worlds, and it is on the website only, never in
          the game.

        h2.legal__h The VR game
        p.
          Everything the game remembers about you is stored on your headset:
          your three save slots, the money and tools they hold, which finds you
          have recovered, quest progress, and your comfort and audio settings.
          None of it is transmitted anywhere. We cannot see it, and we have no
          server that receives it. Uninstalling the game removes it.
        p.
          The game contains no advertising, no analytics, no crash-reporting
          service and no social features. It makes no network requests of its
          own except when you send us feedback, described next.

        h2.legal__h Feedback you send us
        p.
          The settings menu has a "Send Feedback" panel: a short questionnaire
          about your experience, including whether you felt any motion sickness
          and whether you had difficulty with the controls. It is never sent for
          you: you open it, you answer, and nothing leaves the headset until you
          press Send. If you never open it, the game never contacts us at all.
        p.
          When you do send it, this is everything that goes with your answers,
          which reach us as option identifiers — the choices you tapped, not
          words:
        ul.legal__list
          li a random install identifier, created on your headset
          li the build version of the game
          li your device model and operating system version
          li the interface language you have selected
          li how long the session had been running
          li.
            a small set of progress and frame-rate figures: which world you
            were in, your in-game money and lifetime finds, and how smoothly
            the game was running
        p.
          That last group exists so that a report about a problem is actionable
          without you having to describe your setup.
        p.
          The install identifier is a random number and nothing else: it is not
          your Meta account, your Steam ID, your name, your email, or your
          headset's serial number, and it lets us do one thing only — tell two
          reports from the same player apart, so a follow-up makes sense. Your
          IP address reaches our server, as it must for any connection, and we
          use it to stop flooding, but we do not store it with your feedback or
          write it to the feedback log.

        h2.legal__h What we deliberately do not collect
        ul.legal__list
          li your name, email address or any other contact detail
          li your Meta account identifier, Meta username or Steam ID
          li your headset's serial number or device unique identifier
          li.
            your location, IP-derived or otherwise, beyond what is inherent in
            making any internet request at all
          li any advertising or cross-app tracking identifier
        p.
          None of these would tell us anything the random install identifier
          does not, and every one of them would be identity we would then have
          to justify holding.

        h2.legal__h Where feedback is kept, and for how long
        p.
          Feedback is sent to an endpoint we operate and stored on a private
          volume hosted in Australia, with access restricted to the developer.
          We use it solely to improve the game: we do not advertise to you,
          sell it, or share it with anyone outside the small team working on
          the game.
        p.
          Submissions are kept for 24 months from the date you send them and
          then deleted. You can ask us to delete yours sooner — see below.

        h2.legal__h The licence check
        p.
          When the game starts, it asks the Meta platform software on your
          headset a single question: whether the Meta account signed in there is
          entitled to run Buried Worlds — that is, whether it was bought or
          invited to a test release. Meta requires this check of apps on its
          store. It is answered on the device by Meta's own software, tells us
          nothing about who you are, and produces no record that we receive or
          keep.

        h2.legal__h The stores
        p
          | Buying, downloading and running an app from the Meta Horizon Store
          | is handled by Meta, not by us. Anything Meta collects in the
          | process — your purchase, your account, playtime, crash information —
          | is governed by #[a(href="https://www.meta.com/legal/privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") Meta's privacy policy] and their settings, not ours.
          | Meta may give us aggregate figures such as install counts or
          | anonymous crash reports. Where it does, we use them only to
          | understand how the game is performing and to fix faults, and they do
          | not identify individual players to us.
        p
          | The same will be true of Steam when the PC VR version is released:
          | Valve is the data controller for anything collected in buying,
          | installing or running the game there, under
          | #[a(href="https://store.steampowered.com/privacy_agreement/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") Valve's privacy policy],
          | and we receive only aggregate sales and store reporting that does
          | not identify individual players.
        p.
          No third-party analytics service and no third-party crash-reporting
          service receives anything from the game itself. If one is ever added,
          it will be named here, and the change published, before the build
          that uses it ships.

        h2.legal__h This website
        p.
          This site asks you for nothing. There is no form, no sign-up and no
          account. Our web host may keep ordinary server logs, which can
          include IP addresses, for security and reliability.
        p.
          We do use Google Analytics to see how many people visit and which
          pages they read, so we know whether anyone is finding the game. It
          sets cookies in your browser and tells Google your IP address, the
          pages you view, roughly where in the world you are, and basic device
          and browser information. We see only aggregate figures — how many
          visits, from which countries, to which pages — never anything that
          identifies you personally, and we make no attempt to work out who
          individual visitors are. What Google itself does with that data is
          governed by
          #[a(href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") Google's privacy policy], not ours.
        p.
          If you would rather not be counted, any browser setting or extension
          that blocks analytics or third-party scripts will stop it, and we do
          not try to detect or defeat them. Google also publishes an official
          #[a(href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") opt-out add-on]
          that works across every site using Analytics. Nothing on this site
          depends on Analytics working — blocking it costs you nothing.
        p.
          Our typefaces are loaded from Google Fonts, which means Google
          necessarily receives your IP address and basic browser information in
          order to serve them. Links to Discord and Reddit take you to those
          services, where their own privacy policies apply — including anything
          you post or share there. Our community is run on Discord, so if you
          join it, Discord holds your account and messages under its terms, not
          ours.

        h2.legal__h Children
        p.
          Buried Worlds is intended for teens and adults, in line with the age
          group declared on the Meta Horizon Store, and is not directed at
          children under 13; we do not knowingly collect anything from them,
          and Meta requires account holders to meet its own minimum age. The
          game collects nothing from anyone, whatever their age. This website
          counts visits through Google Analytics as described above, which it
          does without knowing anything about who is visiting or how old they
          are.

        h2.legal__h Your rights and how to reach us
        p.
          You can ask us for a copy of anything we hold about you, ask us to
          correct it, or ask us to delete it. These rights belong to everyone
          who plays Buried Worlds, wherever in the world you live. We do not
          ask where you are before acting on a request, and we never will.
        p.
          Unless you have sent us feedback, we hold nothing that identifies
          you — your saves are yours, on your own device, and the website
          analytics reach us only as aggregate counts. There is nothing for us
          to show you, correct or erase. You are welcome to ask us to confirm
          that, and we will.
        p.
          If you have sent feedback, the install identifier is the only way to
          find your submissions again, because we hold no identity to look you
          up by. It is shown on the feedback screen inside the game. Send it to
          us and the submissions attached to it will be deleted within 30 days,
          and we will confirm when it is done. You can also stop any further
          collection at any time simply by not sending feedback.
        p
          | Send any privacy question, request or complaint to
          | #[a(href="mailto:privacy@buriedworlds.com") privacy@buriedworlds.com] and we will
          | respond within 30 days; for anything else, the quickest way to
          | reach us is to #[a(href=links.discord target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") ask on Discord].
          | If our response does not satisfy you, you can complain to the data
          | protection authority where you live. We are based in Australia, so
          | you may also contact the Office of the Australian Information
          | Commissioner at
          | #[a(href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") oaic.gov.au].

        h2.legal__h Changes
        p.
          If we add something that changes any of this — an online feature, a
          leaderboard, analytics of our own — we will update this page and the
          date at the top before it ships, not after.

  +footer(links)
